WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Now the Perashah begins at page 63.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:16.000
But actually, the theme of the Perashah, to understand what's going on in the Perashah,

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:28.000
you must go to the end of last Perashah, Lech Lecha, page 60, verse 24.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:50.000
And then read that Abraham was 99 years old when he circumcised himself.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.080
The last pasuk,

00:00:52.440 --> 00:01:03.780
And all his household, including his slaves,

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.600
the circumcised themselves with him.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.040
But another comes to the point.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:16.040
It means that they were circumcised because of him.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.180
Now one minute.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:33.180
One of the most traumatic experiences in the life of Abraham was when at the age of 99, he had to circumcise himself.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:43.180
As a matter of fact, the trauma was so profound that we mention it every day in the Tefillin, you know in the Salah we say,

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:44.160
about the God,

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:47.800
what does it mean?

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.060
it means,

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:51.820
as the Hakamim say,

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.720
that it was so difficult for Abraham,

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.900
to circumcise himself,

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:58.120
that Borei Olam took him,

00:01:59.040 --> 00:01:59.680
with the arm,

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:00.400
took his arm,

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:02.940
and together God and Abraham,

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:07.420
God had to hold his arm,

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.080
so to speak,

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:08.560
steady,

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:09.460
alright,

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.900
and so that he was able,

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.700
to circumcise himself.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.040
And now we understand the last Pasuk.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:17.940
When they saw this

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:19.400
act of Abraham,

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:20.900
everybody,

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.720
everybody

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:28.360
saw this

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.460
kind of

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:31.620
action,

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.360
they circumcised themselves.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:35.980
That's the end of the

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:36.900
parasha today.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.360
Next parasha, it begins

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:43.320
at the third day of the Milah.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.220
Three days later.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:49.600
Chachamim tells us that the third day of the Milah

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.680
is the most painful of all the days.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:55.140
That was a very hot day.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.100
It was in the summer,

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:00.220
probably around the month of July.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:04.860
And he was in one of the hottest places in the world.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.160
Elon Moreh.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.260
That was one of the hottest places in the world.

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:22.360
And now he is in a tent, so hot that he cannot be inside the tent, because it's too hot inside the tent.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:30.360
He cannot be outside the tent, but he is by the entrance. And you know why he is by the entrance?

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:44.360
He cannot be inside, he cannot be outside, he is right by the door. Yes? And something happened.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:57.360
Now, I want you to enter, to penetrate the mind of Abraham Avinu, 99 years old, just circumcised himself in enormous amount of pain.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:14.000
He is weak. He has nobody. God promised him the world. But in point of fact, what does he have? A tent in the middle of the desert. No son, no Isaac yet. Alright?

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:17.300
Sarah was supposed to be the mother of many children.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:20.020
She is a 90 years old lady.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:20.860
Alright?

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:22.080
No hope.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:22.980
Alright?

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:28.940
And he did what people would say one of the craziest things in the world.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:30.040
Yes?

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:31.080
Circumcise yourself.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.000
Now he's in that situation.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:39.460
Vayera elad Adonai Be'erone Mamre.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:46.460
And at the third day, during this moment of anguish, self-examination,

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:53.460
God, Dayera Elav Adonai Be'lone Mamre, God revealed Himself to Abraham.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:57.460
Be'lone Mamre, in the valley of Mamre, where this happened.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:04.460
Be'hu, in Abraham, Yosher B'Petah Ha'ohel.

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:11.460
He is at the entrance and there is, he's not inside, he's not outside, he's petah ha'oel,

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:19.460
kehoma yom, as the day was getting hotter and hotter. And all of a sudden, he has a vision.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:25.460
But he's not enough. He raises his eyes, bayab, and he sees something.

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:30.460
Now, I want you to picture this situation. He's down in the valley, Elone Mamre,

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:40.460
he's in a valley, he raises his eyes and there is a road, and on the road, above his head,

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:49.460
above the horizon, yes, he sees the initial O'Sha'al HaNashim, the three men, Nusabim Ala,

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:58.460
they are standing up on the road, he's down in the valley, and they're standing Nusabim Ala on top of him.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:13.460
Vayyar, and as soon as he sees it, Vayyaros Ligatam bebet ha'oher. He runs from the entrance of the ha'oher, Vayyaros Ligatam, to meet them.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:24.460
I want you to understand the situation very well. He's sitting down here below, above, maybe 20, 30 yards above.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:30.280
He sees three men standing on top of him, and then the men continue on the road.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:35.040
And then, he goes to run to meet them.

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:40.340
He knows that if he would run upwards this way, he's not going to be able to reach them.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:47.360
So he goes diagonally, so that he's going to be able to meet them.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:51.980
What happened to the old man?

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:53.580
To the brave man?

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:56.220
to the man that he was totally exhausted.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:58.140
How this old man

00:06:58.140 --> 00:06:59.340
can't run?

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:00.940
What happened to him?

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.200
He wasn't 100 years old.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:05.900
And he was hurting.

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:06.860
He was hurting.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.480
That is the visit of God.

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:12.280
Vayera el Abaddonai.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:14.180
As he made

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:15.080
circumcision,

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:17.700
a metamorphosis

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:20.120
took place in the body of

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:20.980
Abraham Abednon.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:24.300
He changed. He's no longer old.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:35.460
he could run so fast that not only he could climb the upward elevation,

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:40.460
but moreover he is able to catch up with the travelers.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:43.460
V'y'áros mikratán.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:48.460
And he did this, me petah ha'ohel, he didn't have to walk a few steps and then run.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:52.460
مِبْتَحَ أَوْهِلْ He sprang like a runner.

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:54.460
مِبْتَحَ أَوْهِلْ

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:57.460
بَيَّارُسِكَ تَمْ مِبْتَحَ أَوْهِلْ

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:00.460
Now you understand the transformation in the body of Abraham.

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:07.460
A miracle is the precision, is the miracle of rejuvenation, a new birth.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:11.460
Yes? And that's the, that's the image that we have here.

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:13.460
right?

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:15.460
...

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:17.460
...

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:19.460
and when he sees them, he bowed down

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:21.460
to them. Now one of the

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:23.460
great

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.460
discoveries

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:27.460
of Abraham, was

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:29.460
that he discovered the unity of God.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.460
That's great.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:33.460
Discovered that there is a God in the universe, Creator, etc.

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:35.460
That's great.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:37.460
But people do not understand

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:39.460
what we mean by

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:49.280
knowing that there is a God. If there is a God in the universe, and if every individual is created

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:57.760
Beselem Elohim in the image of God, this belief should be translated in a certain kind of relationship,

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:05.780
attitude towards our fellow humans. The great discovery of Abraham Avinu was not only that there is a God,

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:15.780
But because there is a God, our relationship should be different. And you see it here in the Misbah that he instituted.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:25.780
He invented a Misbah, the Misbah of Akhenasat Orhim, that you see a poor wayfarer, yes, traveling in the desert.

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:29.780
You don't know him, you never saw him before, you will never see him again.

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:35.940
that you do something that is part of the Hebrew mentality today, thanks to Abraham,

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:40.220
you do something for the sake of goodness.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:45.400
And then when he meets them, they say, hey you, would you like to have a glass of water?

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.200
He bows down to them.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:51.060
He greets them.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:55.960
The notion of treating the stranger not as an enemy,

00:09:55.960 --> 00:10:02.160
but as somebody whom you respect, treating somebody with respect.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:08.360
Normally, when we bring a poor into our home, yes, if we bring a poor into our home,

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:13.960
we treat this person sometimes with deference, and sometimes with not, not with deference.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:16.560
Sometimes we treat them like second class, and so on.

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:19.960
What's the importance here of Abraham Avinu was teaching us,

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:23.920
That's why we can, such a powerful people, such an extraordinary people is,

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:29.240
You respect your fellow men.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.000
You respect other people.

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:35.800
And now he speaks to them and says,

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:39.100
By your mouth, Adonai, my Lord,

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:44.400
If I find grace in your eyes,

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:48.280
He addresses himself to them.

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:52.320
all those persons who says, do not pass me by. Now, here again,

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:56.520
normally, you will ask, I mean, the poor person

00:10:56.520 --> 00:11:00.580
will ask the wealthy person, may I have something

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:04.560
from you? Would you do me a favor and give me a glass of

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:08.560
water? Would you do me a favor and let me stay by the shade of your tree?

00:11:09.420 --> 00:11:12.460
In the case of Abraham Avinu, he asks them

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:16.340
that they should do him a favor. And from here,

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:20.480
says, Gadol is greater the favor that the

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:24.540
oreach makes to the pahalapayit than what the pahalapayit makes to the oreach.

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:28.540
Or, in other words, it's greater the favor that the poor

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:31.760
makes to the rich than what the rich does to the poor.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:35.820
That's the whole idea. It's not only charity. It's not charity in the vulgar

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:39.640
Western Christian sense, you know, with

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:41.400
patronizing somebody.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:44.360
imna basati hem ve'einecha

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:46.160
al nata avor

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:47.120
me'al avdecha

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:49.760
please, would you let me

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:52.000
invite you to my home

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:52.820
alright

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:56.520
and now he says

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:58.020
yukachna me'at mayu

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:00.880
I'm going to give you a little bit of water

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:02.980
ve'lachasurak lechem

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:03.800
so that you could

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:05.140
wash your feet

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:07.840
ve'isha'anu tahana'ez

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:10.580
and rest under the tree

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:20.580
Now, one of the earmarks of the sattik, the haqqani say sattik, omer mi'ad, le'ose harbe.

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:26.580
Rish'eim omerim harbe, le'ose shum davat. You know, that's the point, that's what the haqqani say.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:35.580
Here, what he said, I'm not going to give you much, just let me give you, you kahnameh at mind, a little bit of water.

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:38.580
and rest under the tree. Alright?

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:41.580
And that's not going to do much more than that.

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:44.580
Now, the kapat hem,

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:47.580
I'm going to give you a loaf of bread,

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:50.580
and sa'adu lepehem,

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:53.580
you strengthen with food, sa'adu means

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:56.580
you nourish your heart,

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:59.580
and then you continue on your journey.

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:02.580
ki alkena abartem ala dehem

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:04.740
to him, to say, pass to the house

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:06.440
of your slave.

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:10.120
And they answered,

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:16.880
Do what you said.

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:18.040
Now,

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:20.900
Abraham is no longer old,

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:22.960
he's no longer 99 years old,

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:24.640
he's no longer a just circumcised

00:13:24.640 --> 00:13:26.720
person, he's a young man.

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:28.640
By my hand, Abraham,

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:30.120
and Abraham

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.320
rushes,

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.360
he goes

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:35.740
to the tent of Saram.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:38.760
By Yom HaMaharim.

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:39.920
Quickly!

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:42.300
HaKhlasad Rahim. Because the whole

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.960
notion of HaKhlasad Rahim, that's why it's so great,

00:13:44.020 --> 00:13:45.940
HaKhlasad Rahim, because it's a

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:48.280
partnership between husband and wife.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.000
The husband cannot do it by himself,

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.100
the wife cannot do it by herself. It's a

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:54.260
partnership. And here we have the first

00:13:54.260 --> 00:13:56.920
case in history of HaKhlasad Rahim

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:57.520
we have it here.

00:13:58.140 --> 00:13:59.460
This is the case of that.

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:00.460
He says,

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:03.460
Yes?

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:04.460
Yes?

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:13.460
Take like, I don't know, four gallons of fine flour,

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:16.460
loosing, knead them,

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:19.460
and make, oh God, I want this cake.

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:22.460
Like the pita, like the Arabic pita, you know?

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:25.460
That's exactly what it means, right?

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:32.460
Now, while his wife, she's baking the, preparing the bread for the, for the wayfarers,

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:38.460
Ve'lach bakar ras Abraham, Abraham goes to the place where he had the cows,

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:45.460
and he takes, Ve'ikach ben bakar rach batot, he takes a very tender cap,

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:51.460
by tender knife, he gives it to his servant, by mahelas, or the dog, to do it very quickly.

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:56.460
So, Haram Izzet, what does it mean to make it very quickly? That he gave him to eat the tongue.

00:14:56.460 --> 00:15:06.460
Do you know why the tongue? No? No? Let's see if anybody knows why the tongue. Why?

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:10.460
Because the tongue is the only part of the animal that you don't need to skin him first.

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:16.460
You see? So he was so peculiar, so that he saw that they were, oh he thought that they were tired,

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:22.220
that He gives them the first thing that He gives them is the tongue, because they don't have to wait until you skin the animal.

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:31.020
You see? Alright? So again, now, Abraham Avinu obviously didn't know at the moment that these people were angels,

00:15:31.020 --> 00:15:34.140
they were special angels of God. That is the vision of God.

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:38.780
There was, how God revealed Himself? Through these wayfarers, alright?

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:42.460
In the way that Abraham Avinu treat them, alright? Yes?

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:45.660
Did He make shaitan? Absolutely, that's what He revealed, that He makes shaitan.

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:52.660
Yes? We have no proof, but we believe that Abraham Abeno meant Shehita, we believe that Abraham Abeno observed the whole Torah.

00:15:52.660 --> 00:16:05.660
Yes, alright, but the point of this, of the story is not so far the Shehita, but it's the way that the concept of religion that we have, which is different, you know,

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:13.620
You know, again, our concept of God has to be implemented and reflected in our behavior towards other human beings.

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:20.420
If somebody does not know how to treat another human being, he doesn't have clear in his mind what we mean by

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:22.260
بِسَلِمِ الْأَحْزَاةَ عَدَى

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:25.440
The origin of Gimut Hasadim is so important.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:30.720
Yeah, and Gimut Hasadim for us is not something that you do with your checkbook.

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:32.700
It's something you do with your body.

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:35.640
You know, like Abraham Avinu, he did it with his body.

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:36.240
Yes?

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:36.980
Personally.

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:38.980
That's the notion of Gimelot Hasadim.

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:44.860
You do Gimelot Hasadim personally, with your body, to serve the body of another person.

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:48.800
It's a direct, it's a body-to-body relationship.

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:49.420
Yes?

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:51.460
Of course, we give tzedakah, we sign a check.

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:51.980
That's nice.

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:52.700
It's beautiful.

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:54.580
But that's not Gimelot Hasadim.

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:56.600
Gimelot Hasadim, that is the case of Abraham Avinu.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:57.260
All right?

00:16:57.260 --> 00:17:02.280
And again, you see, the Hagamim say Gimelot Hasadim and tzedakah.

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:07.700
The agayu could do only to the poor. But gemel chasidim you could do to the poor and to the rich.

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:12.700
These people, anybody traveling, out of town, he's been saying, this is a problem.

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:17.700
Alright? And you took gemel chasidim. I don't know, when you're driving, you go outside and you see somebody,

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:20.700
